Run: what is open, in one place
===============================

After 0.07 (2026-11-08).  Keep this file current: when an item is decided or
done, remove it here and record it where it belongs (Changes, the POD).

A. WAITING FOR THE AUTHOR'S DECISION

 1. A command that only exits non-zero puts "system `CMD': rc=N" into errs
    (printed on STDERR when the caller collects no errs).  sh says nothing
    then, and the status is in $data->{result} anyway.  Act: keep it, or
    report only what kept a command from running.
 2. The messages of the commands of new_or that failed stay in errs when a
    later one succeeds (the POD's TODO).  Act: keep them, or clear them.
 3. Release 0.07 on CPAN (its ZIP is on its download page); Proc-Spawner
    0.09 recommends it.

B. WORK (no decision needed)

 - Win32: a kid's arguments go through Perl's command line, which does not
   quote them as the kid's C runtime parses them back (a bug of Perl's;
   t/win32.t's argv test is TODO until Perl is fixed).  Drafts of the
   report: Proc-Spawner's doc/perl-win32-system-bugs.md.
 - Win32 is tested under Wine only; OS/2 and VMS are not tested at all.
 - Outside Linux and Win32 the close-on-exec flag of a target fd is
   inferred, not read (Perl cannot read it without changing it).
